Title

Update Email-API Test Build to Use Local Docker Builder

Description

Issue:
The Email-API TeamCity pipeline was failing during the Run tests step when building the test container.

The test Dockerfile uses the Email-API image generated during Step 1 as its BASE_IMAGE. Although Step 1 successfully built and imported the image into the TeamCity agent’s local Docker store, Step 2 was using the dkrb01-corp-xm1 remote BuildKit builder.

Because the remote builder could not access the image stored locally on the TeamCity agent, it attempted to resolve the Email-API image from MSR. The image had not yet been pushed to MSR because the registry push occurs after successful testing, resulting in an image not found failure.

Root Cause:
The application image produced in Step 1 was available in the TeamCity agent’s local Docker image store but was not accessible to the remote dkrb01-corp-xm1 builder being used by docker compose build tests.

Change Implemented:
Updated the Run tests build step so that only the test container build uses the TeamCity agent’s default/local Docker builder:
BUILDX_BUILDER=default docker compose build tests

This scopes the builder selection specifically to the test build without changing the builder configuration for the rest of the pipeline or other builds running on the agent.



